 "phases_about": "Per phase (Ben, 28 October; tunnel methods by era): cc_max is the deepest cut and cover (rail depth, m); min_drive the shortest shield drive (m; a judgement, not sourced); deep_from the rail depth of lift or escalator stations. Shield needs one tube diameter of cover over the crown: type A from 10.10 m, the bore from 15.50 m, type C from 10.85 m. Phase 1 cc_max 12.19 m (40 ft, the canon-shallow flag); Phase 2 16.5 m (the bore minimum + 1 m, so the methods overlap); Phase 3 15 m. min_radius: the minimum horizontal radius for station approaches and spacing changes (Ben, 28 October: 40, 55, 70 m).",
 "tbm_about": "phases.tbm (Ben, 31 October: \"deep-bore is a thing when it's TBM\"): running tunnels and mined stations of a phase with tbm are the deep bore by tunnel boring machine, else the hand shield. Phase 3 and later by default (drawing values; set on the hub page)."
